=====

USAGE
The UMD package is a stand-alone collection of executable python scripts.
Compile the C libraries first (see README.txt), then run the scripts from the src folder, e.g.:
    python3 VaspParser.py -f OUTCAR
    python3 gofr_umd.py -f OUTCAR.umd.dat
Every script prints its options with -h.


=====

DEPENDENCIES
python3
numpy
scipy
matplotlib
a C compiler (gcc) for the C libraries


